Rewritten: the provider profile itself (its default base of
https://openpaths.io/v1, its OPENPATHS_API_KEY variable, its curated model
list, and the reasoning_effort mapping its build_api_kwargs_extras method
works out) as a Nodecode catalog row, one /models read and one request-body
hook. The mapping keeps the original's rules: xhigh is sent as high, an
auto-think route with no effort is sent auto, reasoning turned off is sent
none, and a level outside OpenPaths' vocabulary is lowered to the nearest one
it takes rather than passed through.

Added, because Nodecode's catalog is where a picker reads its list: the row
itself, since models.dev publishes no OpenPaths entry, and the /models read
at start and hourly, which the original's profile also did.

Left out, and why: the Hermes seams the original imported (providers.base,
ProviderProfile, register_provider) have no place here, so the profile is a
catalog row and its two methods are one /models read and one request-body
hook. The provider aliases (openpath, open-paths, open-path) have no
Nodecode equivalent, where a provider id is matched exactly. The original's
default_aux_model of auto-easy-task is not written into anyone's config by
the cell: the auxiliary target is the operator's pick in /models. The
OPENPATHS_BASE_URL variable becomes the section's base_url, the one place
Nodecode reads an address from.
